::JOUR_U01_L03_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] Which transition best shows technology changing journalism distribution? {
=A. Printed bulletin to mobile news alert#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. Student opinion to private diary#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Source interview to invented quote#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. Caption to unrelated slogan#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_Q02::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] Why did websites change student journalism? {
~A. They remove the need for editors.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. They allow updates to reach audiences faster than print alone.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~C. They make every source reliable.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. They prevent corrections.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_Q03::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] A podcast can change journalism by allowing audiences to: {
~A. avoid facts completely#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. replace reporting with rumors#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. hear source voices and replay interviews#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. remove context from quotes#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_Q04::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] What risk comes with very fast digital publishing? {
~A. Audiences cannot access updates.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. Reporters cannot use sources.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Headlines become impossible.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=D. Errors can spread quickly if facts are not verified.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_Q05::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] A design trend toward short mobile posts means journalists should: {
=A. write clear concise updates that still use verified facts#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. skip all source checking#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. use only dramatic images#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. hide the main information#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
