~A. uses random slides without focus#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. contains only decoration#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. organizes coherent verified ideas for an audience#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. has no source information#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_Q07::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] Which answer explains both opportunity and responsibility? {
~A. Mobile alerts are fast, so accuracy matters less.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. Mobile alerts reach students quickly, so facts must be confirmed before sending.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
